    'nuances' => array(
        'Never downgrade a predictive claim to an alerting one. English "predict failures", "forecast", "anticipate" is 预测故障 / 预判故障 (keep the object); 预警 means early warning and may be used ONLY where the English itself says alert/warn/notify. The same class: 诊断 stays 诊断 (not 提示), 检测 stays 检测 (not 提醒). Downgrading the verb sells a materially smaller product than the English does.',
        'Do not calque English "maximize / minimize" as a transitive Chinese verb. "maximize the value of your equipment" is 充分释放设备价值 (or 充分发挥设备价值), never 最大化设备价值; "minimize costs" is 尽可能降低成本, never 最小化成本. Chinese uses a verb phrase with 充分／尽可能, and 最大化／最小化 belong to maths and engineering optimisation, not marketing copy.',
        'Every question label inside one form must take the same shape. If any label is nominalised ("What type of request is this?" → 请求类型), nominalise them all — 请求优先级, 请求类型, 设备型号或类型 — and do not leave one sibling as a full question (此请求的优先级是什么？). Decide the shape once per form and apply it to every label in that form.',
        'When the branch or business-unit name inside a label already contains 咨询 ("consulting"), rename that element rather than the suffix: "Support & consulting sales inquiry" is 支持与顾问服务销售咨询. The 销售咨询 suffix must stay byte-identical across every sibling inquiry label (航空航天与工业销售咨询, 交通运输与汽车销售咨询) and the honorific 垂询 must never appear on a clickable label, tab or option value.',
        'Treat OBD, NVH, HVAC, ADAS, NDT, BaaS as a fixed set and render each the same way on every surface — nav label, footer, menu card, article headline and body. If the nav says OBD 咨询与培训, an article headline must also say OBD (OBD 不仅用于汽车：…), never expand it to 车载诊断系统 in one place while abbreviating it in another. One acronym rendered two ways across the same site is a visible two-pass tell.',
        'Refrigeration and HVAC: English "vapor" in a thermodynamic cycle is 蒸气, never 蒸汽 (which is steam). "Vapor compression cooling" is 蒸气压缩式制冷; "vapor recovery" is 蒸气回收. Reserve 蒸汽 strictly for actual steam equipment (蒸汽锅炉、蒸汽管道).',
        'When English "machine" modifies data/analytics/monitoring, translate the OBJECT of the analysis, not the word: "machine analytics" is 设备数据分析, "machine health analytics" is 设备健康分析, "machine data" is 设备数据. Bare 机器分析 parses as "mechanical/机械 analysis" and hides the equipment-monitoring product. Use the same 设备… term in the nav label, the menu card and the body copy — a nav that says 机器分析 beside body copy that says 设备健康分析 proves two passes.',
        'Corporate capability statements take a neutral adverb, never a warm personal one: 由打造这些测试系统的团队直接提供, not 亲自提供. 亲自 (in person / personally) belongs to an individual doing a favour and over-personalises a systems claim; the same applies to 倾情、用心、贴心 in B2B equipment copy.',
        'Never open two consecutive sentences with the same demonstrative. If 这一 has just started the previous sentence, use 该 (or drop the demonstrative) in the next: 这一互联的性能管理解决方案……。该有效工具输出的数据…… Vary 这一／该／此类 across a paragraph and keep every modifier (有效) and the verb (输出) intact when you do.',
        'Keep the engineering colour of "engineer" used as a verb by an engineering company. "we engineer new possibilities" is 我们以工程之力开创新的可能 or 我们通过工程实现……, never bare 开创／打造, which reads as generic marketing. Same for "we architect" (以架构设计实现), "we machine" (以机加工实现).',
        'For the participial frame "In a strategic move reflecting its commitment to X, Y announced…", keep the appositive reading (an existing commitment, never a purpose frame with 为体现……) but do NOT stack it in front of the head noun. Split it: 作为一项战略举措，Y 宣布……，彰显其……的一贯承诺。 — never 作为体现其……承诺的战略举措，Y 宣布…… Apply the same split to any English frame that puts a relative clause ahead of 举措／方案／计划.',
        'Translate EVERY string a consent/cookie component prints from its config payload, not only the banner sentences: table headers (名称／域名／有效期), the singular and plural count words ("cookie"/"cookies" → 项 Cookie), the Privacy Policy link label (隐私政策), every aria-label (Cookie consent → Cookie 同意设置) and any legal disclosure sentence — e.g. the cross-border transfer notice: 同意记录还可能发送至本网站配置的数据处理方，该处理方可能位于其他国家/地区。 A Chinese dialog wrapped around an English table is the most visible half-translation on the site, and it is the panel PIPL-minded legal and procurement readers open.',
        'A one-word English nav category is often a clipped technical compound — expand it to the full Chinese industry term instead of translating the clipped word. In an HVAC/refrigeration menu "Climate" means climate CONTROL, so "Climate & energy" is 暖通制冷与能源 (or 温控与能源 where the label must be short), never 气候与能源, which a Chinese reader parses as the meteorology/climate-change/ESG sector. Same trap: "Power" in a driveline menu is 动力总成, "Vision" in an inspection menu is 机器视觉.',
        'Utility and wayfinding nav labels stay plain and literal; do not lift them into marketing register. "Locations" is 全球基地 / 基地 (a list of places), never 全球布局, which promises a strategic-footprint story and hides the address directory a capital-equipment buyer is hunting for. Reserve 布局／版图／战略 for headings and body copy, never for a directory link.',
        'Never translate a hortative English CTA with 让我们 + verb — it is a calque that no Chinese CTA uses. "Let\'s talk" is 洽谈合作 (or 联系我们), "Let\'s get started" is 立即开始, "Join us" is 加入我们. Use a verb-object imperative, and if a sibling string already renders 联系我们 ("Contact Us"), pick the other option so two different English CTAs stay distinct.',
        '"Integrate / bring it all together" in a systems context is 集成 sitewide (将一切集成在一起, 系统集成), never 整合, which means organisational consolidation. Hold one rendering across every surface the same sentence appears on — visible heading, sticky-nav JSON, menu card — and keep the tag form with no half-width spaces: 将一切<span class="textorange">集成</span>在一起.',
        'A Chinese verb must not be left dangling when the English verb carries an implied object. "allowing us to adapt swiftly" is 使我们能够迅速应变 (or 迅速适应客户需求的变化), never the objectless 迅速适应, which trails off mid-sentence. Read every finished clause back: 适应、响应、提升、改善、满足 all require a stated object in Chinese even where English can drop it.',
        'Localise the units and column headers of any generated data table (cookie/consent tables, spec tables), not just the descriptive sentences beside them. Durations take Chinese units — "2 years" is 2 年, "30 minutes" is 30 分钟, "1 day" is 1 天, "3 months" is 3 个月, "session" is 会话期间 — and headers are 名称／域名／有效期. An English duration column sitting beside Chinese descriptions makes the panel visibly half-translated.',
        'aria-label navigation landmarks must name the region, not copy the English adjective: "Primary" is 主导航 and "Mobile primary" is 移动端主导航 — never 主要 (bare adjective) and never 移动端优先, which means the mobile-first design philosophy. Any one-word landmark label (Primary, Secondary, Footer, Utility) takes 导航 as its head noun.',
        'Translate sibling UI controls as a SET, never string-by-string. Previous/Next must land on one noun axis — 上一个／下一个 (or 上一张／下一张 for image sliders) — never 上一页 paired with 下一步. Same for 展开／收起, 显示更多／显示更少. One arrow saying 页 while its twin says 步 is the classic segment-in-isolation MT signature.',
        'A Chinese UI command needs a complete object: "Download Chat" is 下载聊天记录, "Clear Chat" is 清空聊天记录, "Export" is 导出记录. Never leave the English bare noun as the object (下载聊天) — Chinese verbs require the full nominal.',
        'Consent and privacy controls must be reordered into Chinese verb-first form, not left with English word order: "Google Analytics Opt Out" is 退出 Google Analytics 跟踪, "Privacy opt-out controls" is 隐私选择退出设置, "Manage cookie preferences" is 管理 Cookie 偏好设置. Never end a clickable label with a trailing 选择退出, and use 设置 (not 控制) for a preferences panel.',
        'CCPA/GDPR-style links that express a user instruction take the negative imperative: "Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information" is 请勿出售或分享我的个人信息, not the flat descriptive 不出售或分享我的个人信息. If the English is an imperative the reader issues to the company, keep it an imperative in Chinese.',
        'In a chat or contact widget, "message" is 消息, never 信息 (which a reader parses as "your information/details"), and input placeholders take the polite imperative: 请输入您的消息……, 请输入您的姓名. Apply 请 + verb to every placeholder in the set.',
        '"Aftermarket" as a sales channel is 售后市场 everywhere — nav, footer and body (ADAS 校准售后市场系统, ADAS 售后市场). 售后 alone means after-sales service and must not stand in for the channel. Fix the concept sitewide, not the one label the reviewer happened to see.',
        'Delete redundant temporal adverbs when a 在…前 clause already carries the advance sense: 在故障发生前预警, never 在故障发生前提前预警. The same applies to 提前预先, 事先预判, 再次重复 — read the finished clause back and cut the second marker.',
        'When two senses of one word collide in a compound label, break the collision by changing the HEAD NOUN, never by switching register: "Support & consulting sales inquiry" is 支持与咨询业务销售咨询 (业务 separates 咨询 from 咨询), not 咨询服务销售咨询 and never 垂询, which is honorific company-voice and must never appear on a clickable label, tab or option value.',
        '"Available X" in a menu of purchasable options goes predicate-final: 多种服务级别协议可选, not the pre-modifier 可选服务级别协议, which can be read as "the SLA is optional". Never use 可用, which misparses as an availability (uptime) SLA.',
        'Replace 来自……的 + long pre-modifier with a Chinese verb: 这一有效工具输出的数据, not 来自这一有效工具的数据; 该平台记录的设备数据, not 来自该平台的设备数据. Keep the English modifier (有效) and keep the verb\'s valence exactly as neutral as the English — 产生显著影响 stays neutral; never upgrade to 改善／减少／优化 even when a reviewer suggests it.',
        'Mark who submits a request. "support requests for Bauer customers and other partners" means requests FROM them: Bauer 客户及其他合作伙伴提交的支持请求. 对……的支持请求 reverses the direction to requests aimed AT those customers. Check the agent on every English "for/from" noun phrase in service and form copy.',
        'Keep SLA, priority and intake-form definitions in plain functional register — no 成语. "immediate safety risk" is 紧迫的安全风险 (urgency axis, functional), never the literary 迫在眉睫的安全风险 and never 直接的安全风险 (which shifts to the directness/importance axis). Reserve idioms for marketing blocks.',
        'Keep "Read More" and "Learn More" distinct on every surface: news/article cards take 阅读全文 (or 阅读文章), section and banner CTAs take 了解更多, announcements take 查看公告. One Chinese CTA doing duty for two different English CTAs flattens a distinction the source makes.',
        'Use the doubled full-width ellipsis …… in EVERY placeholder of a set, not just the one that was reviewed: 搜索……, 请输入您的消息……. A single U+2026 beside a doubled one in a sibling search box is a visible typographic inconsistency.',
        'In turbocharger and rotating-assembly contexts, English "core" means the CHRA / cartridge and must be 芯体 (涡轮增压器芯体 / 芯体总成), NOT 铁芯. Reserve 铁芯 strictly for the laminated iron core of an electric machine, and only when the surrounding page is clearly about motors/stators. When a balancer brand sits beside 柴油涡轮增压器动平衡 or 涡轮增压器动平衡系统 on the same page, "Core Balancing Machine" is 芯体动平衡机 (e.g. CMT-TR 低速芯体动平衡机).',
        'Never use the honorific 垂询 as a clickable label, tab, button or option value. 垂询 means "your esteemed enquiry to us" and is only idiomatic in company-voice invitations (欢迎垂询). Any "... sales inquiry" label is 销售咨询, applied identically across every sibling in a parallel set — accept a mild 咨询…咨询 repetition rather than switching register on one item of a list (支持与咨询服务销售咨询, not 支持与咨询服务销售垂询).',
        'Translate support/service "case" as 工单 (or 案件), never 案例. 案例 means a case study or worked example; in an intake form 这是什么类型的案例？ reads as "what kind of case study is this?". Write 这属于哪类工单？. Reserve 案例/案例研究 exclusively for marketing case studies.',
        'Severity words must be translated on the severity axis, never the importance axis. "Critical issue" in an SLA or priority definition is 严重故障 / 紧急故障, never 关键问题 (关键 = key/pivotal). Likewise "immediate safety risk" is 迫在眉睫的安全风险, not 直接安全风险 (直接 = direct).',
        '性能 describes a machine, system or component. Never attach it to a company, business or market noun: "unlock the performance of your business" is 充分释放您的业务潜能 / 释放企业的业绩潜能, never 释放您业务的性能潜力. Business-level performance takes 业绩、效能、潜能、表现.',
        'Counter and stat labels for "home countries" must not become 本土国家 — 本土 (one\'s own native soil) cannot pluralise across foreign countries. Render the claim as a predicate: 个国家设有本土团队 (local presence) or 个国家/地区开展业务 (reach). Same pattern for "global locations": prefer 个全球基地 with the scope adverb outside the measure phrase if it reads awkwardly.',
        'Never open a Chinese sentence with a bare 或 copied from an English "Or ..." sentence. Use 或者，… or fold the clause into the preceding sentence with 若…，亦属此类.',
        'Never repeat the same disyllabic noun twice inside one short clause. 在故障发生前预判故障 must become 在故障发生前提前预警 or 防患于未然. Read every finished clause back and delete the second occurrence.',
        'Adverbials of duration attached to a demonstration verb stay with that verb. "Watch how we integrate X, Y and Z ... in a few minutes" is 用几分钟时间，观看我们如何将…集成…, never 观看我们如何在几分钟内将…集成…, which claims the integration itself takes minutes — an incredible engineering claim.',
        '"Gauging" in a capability list (assembly / balancing / functional test / NVH / gauging / calibration) is dimensional gauging: 尺寸检测 or 量规检测. Do not render it 测量, which both flattens the term and collides with the division name 测试与测量.',
        'An English participial frame "In a strategic move reflecting its commitment to X, Y announced…" describes an EXISTING commitment. Translate it as an appositive: 作为体现其…承诺的战略举措，Y 宣布… . Never use 为体现…的承诺 (= "in order to demonstrate"), which turns substance into image management.',
        'Convert English passives and nominal parallels into active Chinese. "people are empowered to" is 人们获得赋能、敢于… not 人们被赋予能力去…; "trusts it will be safe, reliable, and excel in performance" is 相信它安全可靠、性能卓越, not the 的、的，并…出众 chain. Avoid 被 unless the agent genuinely matters.',
        'Automotive "turbo" is always 涡轮增压器; bare 涡轮 means turbine and must be reserved for aerospace turbine/jet-engine contexts. Never let the two share one word on the same site (Cimat 涡轮增压器动平衡系统 vs 涡轮机与喷气发动机动平衡).',
        '"Actuation" in aerospace is 作动 / 作动系统 (作动器). 执行机构 belongs to process-control valves and must not be used for landing-gear or flight-control actuation.',
        'Verbs like "featuring", "powered by", "built around" need a real Chinese verb, not 采用…的: "Test stands featuring Bauer" is 搭载 Bauer 技术的测试台.',
        'Pick ONE Chinese noun per English facility/label word and hold it sitewide: "location" is 基地 everywhere (Three Rivers 基地总经理, 个全球基地) — never 工厂, which asserts a manufacturing plant the English does not claim; "assembly" is 装配 everywhere, never 组装; "marketplace" is 备件商城 everywhere, never 在线商城; "form" is 表单 everywhere, never 表格.',
        'Hold News=新闻 and Press=新闻稿 as a fixed pair on every surface — nav label, card badge (新闻稿 · 2026 年 9 月 22 日) and "See all press" (查看全部新闻稿). Never let a Press badge render 新闻 while the News nav also reads 新闻.',
        'Do not reduce a named platform to a tool. When the surrounding copy calls the offering a 平台, "Analytics that deliver timely insights" is 提供及时洞察的分析平台, not 分析工具.',
        'Form microcopy must be written as native Chinese UI, not as translated English sentences: <select> placeholder "Select an option" is 请选择 (never 选择一个选项); "What type of request is this?" is 请求类型; "Any error codes from the system you can share?" is 可否提供系统报出的错误代码？; "This requires the scheduling of service" folds into the preceding clause as 需安排服务…, not 这需要安排….',
        'Use full-width ／ for every slash inside Chinese copy (轻微磨损／损伤, 校准／认证, 州／省份) — a single ASCII / among full-width siblings is a visible inconsistency. Never leave an orphan half-width space where a separator belongs: a document title before 白皮书 takes 书名号 (《HVAC 空气处理机组精密动平衡》白皮书).',
        'Drop the perfective 了 from general-capability claims. "streamlines validation, improves throughput" is 简化验证流程、提高吞吐量, not 简化了…、提高了…, which reports a completed past event instead of a standing capability.',
        'Use written, not spoken, positional words in UI copy: 上方的 / 下方的, never 上面的 / 下面的.',
        'Freight trailers are 挂车, not 拖车 (which reads as a tow truck in Mainland usage): "refrigerated trailers" is 冷藏挂车.',
        '"Available SLAs" is 可选服务级别协议. 可用 misparses as an availability SLA (an uptime metric), which is a live concept in this product category — use 可选 for menus of purchasable options.',
        'Instructions that tell the visitor to CHOOSE among several forms must keep the choosing: "select from the forms below" is 从下方选择相应表单填写, never 填写下方表单, which erases the routing instruction on a page with multiple form tabs.',
        'Keep B2B register plain and industrial — no literary flourishes. "sharp minds" is 顶尖人才 (汇聚 collocates with 人才/资源, never 头脑); "Blog - featuring audio editions" is 博客（含音频版）, using 括号 rather than an em dash.',
        'Headline pairs of the shape "Elevating support, Enhancing value" need Chinese head nouns on both objects: 提升支持水平，增强客户价值 — not the bare 提升支持，增强价值.',
        'When an English sentence puts an example after a noun phrase ("Standing on the shoulders of our many brands, like Burke Porter, we…"), fold the example INSIDE the Chinese modifier: 依托包括 Burke Porter 在内的众多品牌积累，我们… . Never leave 包括 X after the head noun as a stranded apposition.',
        'Nav labels take the shortest natural Chinese form: "Industries served" is 覆盖行业 (or 服务行业) rather than the stiff 服务的行业.',
        'When two English footer strings differ ("About us:" heading vs "Who we are" link), they must differ in Chinese too: heading 关于我们：, link 公司简介. Never let a heading and its own first child render identically.',
        'A rename copula is not a launch. English "is now" sitting between an old logo and a new logo means the company was renamed: translate it 现已更名为 (or 现为), NEVER 现已推出, which means "is now available / now launched". Reserve 现已推出 strictly for "NOW AVAILABLE" on an actual product.',
        'Named offerings are brands even when every word looks translatable. If a phrase is a product/service name in a nav, footer product column or menu card (ADAS Garage, XL Machine, Burke Porter, Cimat, Galileo, Lismar, Titan, Kleinknecht, WinterPark, Bauer, Sentia, Ascentialytics, Ascential Care), keep the WHOLE name in Latin script: ADAS Garage, not ADAS 车库; XL Machine 产品, not XL 机器产品. Never half-translate a brand in one place and keep it in another on the same page.',
        'Place names inside job titles are proper nouns: "General Manager of Three Rivers Location" is Three Rivers 工厂总经理, never 三河地点总经理. A facility is 工厂/基地/园区; 地点 means a spot on a map and must never be the head noun for a plant or an office.',
        'A numeral immediately followed by a count noun REQUIRES a measure word. Animated counter labels are numerals at runtime even though the HTML shows 0: write 个本土国家, 名专业人才, 个全球基地, 个项目 — never the bare noun 本土国家/专业人才/全球基地. Check every stat label in a set; getting three of four right is the classic segment-by-segment MT signature.',
        'Never change the noun a statistic counts. countries stays 国家 (not 市场), people stays 人才/人员 (not 团队), locations stays 基地/地点 (not 市场). Changing the counted unit changes the factual claim and inflates it — buyers put these numbers in comparison spreadsheets.',
        'Use shop-floor vocabulary for shop-floor nouns, never office-software vocabulary. In a plant-location hint, "cell" is 工位/生产单元 (never 单元格, a spreadsheet cell), "line" is 生产线 (never 行, a spreadsheet row), "column" is 柱号/立柱 (never 列).',
        'Equipment stops, it does not crash. "Machine down" / "the system is down" is 设备停机 / 机器或系统停机 / 故障停机. 宕机 is IT slang for a crashed server and instantly marks the writer as someone who has never stood on a plant floor.',
        'Never let a clinical or computing sense leak into industrial copy. "production complications" is 生产方面的连带问题 / 生产问题, never 并发症 (a medical comorbidity). "texturing" of mill rolls is 毛化, never 纹理化 (computer-graphics texture mapping). When a word has a dominant sense in another domain, pick the manufacturing term explicitly.',
        'Priority and severity wording must stay inside its own tier. Translate the English severity word literally: "non-urgent" is 非紧急, NOT 低优先级. Never let a Priority 2 card describe itself with the label that belongs to Priority 3 — in an intake form this breaks routing and SLA, not just style.',
        'Steel and metals terms are industry-specific, not compositional. "roll grinding" (grinding the mill rolls) is 轧辊磨削 — 辊磨 means a roller mill, a completely different machine. "Metals" as a vertical is 冶金行业/金属行业, so "Metals automation" is 冶金行业自动化, never 金属自动化. "Roll shop" is 轧辊车间.',
        '"Construction" as an activity is 施工/工程建设, not 建筑 (a building, architecture). "utilities construction" is 公用事业工程建设 — 公用事业建筑 narrows "we build utility infrastructure" to "utility buildings".',
        'Commercial-model modifiers name a service model, not a document. "Contract balancing as-a-service" is 委托动平衡即服务（BaaS）or 代客动平衡服务（BaaS）— 合同 is the paper contract, so 合同动平衡 parses as "balancing of a contract". Keep the distinction from unqualified "balancing-as-a-service" (动平衡即服务), which must stay unqualified.',
        '"Marketplace" as a storefront is 商城/在线商城/交易平台. 市场 is the abstract economic sense, so 备件市场 reads as commentary on the spare-parts market rather than a place to buy parts. Write 备件商城.',
        '"Industries served" means the industries we serve: 服务的行业 / 覆盖行业 / 应用行业. Bare 服务行业 reads as "the service sector" and hides the vertical positioning the nav exists to advertise.',
        '"Affiliates" in a corporate footer means group companies: 关联公司 / 关联机构. 合作伙伴 demotes a sister division to an external third party and misstates the corporate structure.',
        '"Transportation" as a business vertical that builds automotive and commercial-vehicle test systems is 交通运输 (or 汽车与交通). Bare 运输 means freight/haulage, so 运输部门首席技术官 reads "CTO of the Shipping Department". Apply the same term in nav labels, form branches and every executive title.',
        'Never translate one English word twice in the same label. 无损检测 already IS non-destructive testing, so "NDT inspection" is 无损检测（NDT）— never 无损检测（NDT）检测. Same for 咨询…咨询 ("consulting" + "inquiry" must take different words: 咨询服务 + 垂询) and 新闻…新闻稿 (use 动态 for "news" beside 新闻稿 for "press"). Read every finished label back and delete any repeated morpheme.',
        'When a label wraps a brand in <span class="tmm-brand-word">, ONLY the brand belongs inside that span. Never extend the span over the descriptor — the brand styling then bleeds across the whole card and breaks visual parity with its siblings.',
        'Chinese machines 做/作 a motion, they do not 执行 one (执行 = execute a command). "What kind of motion does a rigid rotor perform?" is 刚性转子旋转时做何种运动？ Check every verb-object pair against real Chinese engineering writing before shipping.',
        'Never leave an English prepositional or comitative tail as a bare fragment. "…, with machine health analytics from the team that builds the test systems" cannot become 借助……的分析。 with no predicate. Give the tail its own clause: ；设备健康分析由打造这些测试系统的团队亲自提供。 Likewise a verb must keep its object: "Predict failures" is 预判故障, never bare 预测.',
        'Never stack three 的 in one modifier chain. 构建测试系统的团队提供的设备健康分析 is the single most reliable MT tell in Chinese — split it into a separate predicate clause instead.',
        'Rewrite English question word order into Chinese topic-comment. "How can we help you today?" is 今天我们能为您提供什么帮助？ not 今天有什么我们可以帮助您的吗？. "What\'s new at X?" is a noun phrase, X 最新动态, not X 的最新动态是什么？. "Searching <site>" labels a scope, 在 <site> 中搜索, not the progress state 正在搜索. "Looking for X?" is 正在寻找 X 吗？ — never the bare progressive calque 在寻找.',
        'Chinese job titles are strictly left-branching: the department qualifier precedes the title. "Vice President of Global Sales, Aerospace & Industrials" is 航空航天与工业部门全球销售副总裁 — never keep the English trailing comma-clause as ……副总裁，航空航天及工业部门.',
        'Never insert half-width spaces around an inline <span> or <a> inside a Chinese sentence. Write 将一切<span>整合</span>在一起, not 将一切 <span>整合</span> 在一起. The Chinese-to-Latin thin space applies only where real Latin text or digits sit next to Chinese, never at a pure tag boundary.',
        'Pick ONE rendering per term and per connector for the whole site, then never vary it: 测功机 (not 动力计) for dyno, 校准 (not 标定) for calibration, 监测 (not 监控) for monitoring, 无损检测 for NDT, 轧辊磨削 for roll grinding, 与 (not 和) for "&" in nav/menu labels, HVAC (not 暖通空调) once the siblings use HVAC. A term that is right in the footer and wrong in the nav proves two translation passes and is exactly what a technical buyer notices.',
        'Every option inside one <select> must be in the same language. "Bauer | Aerospace" is Bauer | 航空航天 — the brand stays, the sector word does not. One English option beside two Chinese ones is a visible defect in an active form control.',
        'Do not flatten an offer into a capability. "customers have new opportunities to collect, mine and measure data" is 客户得以……采集、挖掘并测量数据，获得全新机遇 — not 客户现在可以. Keep "mine" as 挖掘 (data mining) and "measure" as 测量; rendering mine as 分析 silently swaps a named platform function for one that is already listed.',
        'Do not rhetorically upgrade a flat coordination. "is a promise and our standard" is 既是承诺，也是我们的标准 — the 不仅……更是 escalation strengthens a claim the English never makes. Good copywriting that changes claim strength is still a fidelity error.',
        'Use the settled Chinese compound, not the English word order: "mission-critical" is 任务关键型, never 关键任务型.',
        'Never open a sentence with a subjectless participial clause copied from English. "In a strategic move reflecting its commitment to X, Y announced…" becomes 为体现……的承诺，Y 作出战略举措，宣布…… — the middle clause must have a subject or be folded into a purpose phrase.',
        'Use full-width ellipsis …… inside Chinese strings, never ASCII "..." (输入您的信息……, not 输入您的信息...).',
        'Translate every descriptive word in alt text and check it against the image: "on a transparent background" is 透明背景, not 白色背景 — a wrong background colour in alt text contradicts the sentence it sits in.',
        'In rotor balancing, "core" is the laminated 铁芯 (armature/rotor core), not 芯轴 (a mandrel/arbor, which is tooling). Translate the component the machine actually works on; when unsure between two specific parts, use the generic term rather than guessing.',
        'Use manufacturing vocabulary, not office or spreadsheet vocabulary: a factory "cell" is "生产单元" or "工位", never "单元格"; a production "line" is "生产线".',
        'Keep every modifier, including trailing purpose phrases such as "for their consumers" ("为其消费者").',
        'Count the characters in every pre-nominal modifier before shipping. If more than about 12 characters sit before the head noun, put the noun first and move the modifier into its own predicate clause: 系统专为…定制设计，满足… not 针对…定制设计的系统; 制造商信赖我们，能在…交付… not 深受…结果的制造商信赖. Conventional credential chains (X大学Y专业学士学位) are exempt.',
        'Read every stacked modifier aloud and check for false word boundaries. If two adjacent characters fuse into an unintended word (需要大规模可靠 → 大规模可靠), rebuild with a separate clause such as 在大规模生产中.',
        'Keep the English claim direction and modality exactly. Neutral verbs stay neutral — impact is 产生影响, never 减少/改善/优化/提升 unless the English names that direction — and modals survive as 可/能/有助于, never as a bare assertion of accomplished fact.',
        'Do not re-grade claim strength or invent metrics. optimal for = 最适用于/理想适用于, not 适用于; improved detection = 更出色的缺陷检测, not 缺陷检出率. Never add 率、度、倍 or any quantifiable measure the English does not state, and never upgrade 信息/输入 to 洞察.',
        'Lock the vendor\'s named capabilities to fixed terms: measure is always 测量, matching 测试与测量 — never 分析 or 衡量. Keep 无损检测（NDT） glossed on first mention and NDT thereafter, and use 专用 (not 专业) for dedicated or specialized equipment.',
        'Preserve every separately asserted attribute as its own predicate. Do not fuse two coordinated nouns into one idiomatic compound: proximity and responsiveness must both stand (贴近客户、快速响应), not collapse into 就近响应.',
        'Verify each verb-object pair against native collocation. 汇聚/集结 takes 人才、资源、智慧, never 头脑; 优化 takes 流程、配置, never 需求; 应对/迎接 takes 挑战, 解决 takes 问题/难题. When the English verb is vague, pick the Chinese verb the object actually demands.',
        'Do not calque English quantifier phrases onto concrete nouns. a wide range of / across many becomes 各类、多种、各种, not 广泛的 plus a locative 在…上. Keep proper entity and business-unit names in their source form unless an official Chinese name exists for that exact entity.',
        'FIDELITY: English \'can significantly impact\' is directionally neutral — it claims influence, not improvement. The Chinese assigns a specific favourable outcome to each list item: 减少 (reduce) unplanned downtime, 改善 (improve) machine health, 优化 (optimise) needed repairs. A neutral capability statement has been converted into a three-part performance promise the English never makes. The Turkish rendering (\'öne',
        'FIDELITY: \'measure\' is rendered as 分析 (analyse). Measurement is a distinct, named capability for a test-and-measurement vendor, and the platform\'s third listed function has been silently swapped for a different one (analysis, which 挖掘/mine already covers). Turkish correctly keeps \'ölçme\' (measure).',
        'Cap any pre-nominal modifier at roughly 12 characters. If the English has a longer relative clause or participle before the noun, put the noun first and move the modifier into its own predicate clause: write 系统专为…而设计，满足… rather than 为…设计的系统.',
        'Never let a stacked pre-modifier create a false word boundary. Read the modifier aloud: if two adjacent characters fuse into an unintended word (大规模可靠), rebuild the sentence with a separate clause (在大规模生产中…).',
        'Do not attach English adjectives to abstract Chinese nouns such as 可能性、机会、方案 when the adjective describes how you work. Convert them to a verb phrase or move them onto a concrete noun: 以快速、精准的工程实力开创新的可能, not 快速、精准的可能性.',
        'Do not coordinate different categories (people, knowledge, technology, data) under one verb just because English does. Check that the verb fits every object: 汇聚/集结 takes 人才 and 资源, never 头脑; split the list or change the verb.',
        'Verify every verb-object pair against native collocation before shipping. 优化 takes 流程、安排、配置, not 需求; 提升 takes 效率、精度; 降低 takes 频次、成本. When the English verb is vague (impact, address, drive), choose the specific Chinese verb the object actually demands.',
        'Translate academic fields and degrees as complete Chinese discipline names plus 专业, not character-by-character renderings: 组织领导力专业, 工商管理专业, 数据科学专业. Never leave an English abstract noun as a bare clipped stem.',
        '「挑战」只与应对、迎接、直面搭配；英文 solve/tackle a challenge 若指处理具体问题，译为「解决难题／问题」，绝不写「解决挑战」「攻克挑战」。',
        '中心名词前的定语控制在约 12 个汉字以内；更长的修饰成分必须拆为独立短句或后置分句（「……，适用于……」「……——他们……」），不得照搬英文的前置堆叠。',
        '行业缩写首次出现写「中文全称（英文缩写）」，此后全站统一只用中文全称；同一术语不得在不同页面中英混用（如 NDT／无损检测）。',
        '修饰设备、机型、产线时，英文 specialized/dedicated 译「专用」而非「专业」；「专业」只用于形容人员能力或服务水平。',
        '学位、职称、机构名按中文惯例重组为「在<机构>取得/攻读<专业><学位>」，学位名用中文既有译法（Master of Science in X = X 理学硕士），不得逐词直译。',
        '英文抽象名词作中心语时补足为中文双音节名词（possibilities→可能性、capabilities→能力），并把并列形容词改写为动词短语或后置说明，不得直接叠加在单字名词前。',
        '英文以介词短语开头的标题和设问句（About X, have a … question?）按中文主题—述题顺序重写为「遇到／面对……？」，不保留原文语序。',
        '逐条核对动宾搭配是否为中文固有组合：数据用采集／分析（非「衡量」），经验与能力用积累／沉淀（非「汇聚」），不得沿用英文动词的通用对译。',
        'Inside any Chinese sentence use full-width punctuation only — “ ” for quotes, （） for parentheses, ，。、；：？！ — even when the English source shows ASCII " \' ( ). Half-width characters may appear only inside an untranslated Latin run (phone numbers, URLs, product names).',
        'Hard-cap pre-nominal modifiers: never place more than about eight Chinese characters of modifier before 的 + noun. When English stacks a relative clause or several adjectives ahead of a noun, name the noun first and explain after it with a following clause, a 破折号, or a topic-comment structure.',
        'Pick the verb Chinese actually pairs with the noun, not the English verb\'s dictionary equivalent: 应对／迎接挑战 (never 解决挑战), 攻克难题, 满足需求, 积累经验, 开展检测. If the verb-noun pair does not occur in real Chinese industry writing, rewrite the pair.',
        'When English uses a neutral verb (impact, affect, influence, address), Chinese must stay neutral too: use 影响 with an explicit scope (对……产生显著影响) or restructure (在……方面发挥作用). NEVER substitute a directional verb — 减少/提升/改善/优化 — unless the English itself states that direction. Turning "can impact downtime, machine health and repairs" into "reduces downtime, improves health, optimises repairs" invents a three-part performance promise the client never made, and it is the client who has to stand behind it.',
        'Convert English abstract nominalisations into Chinese verb phrases: opportunities to collect → 可采集, new possibilities → 开辟新的可能, our presence → 我们提供. Never attach concrete adjectives such as 快速／毫不妥协／无缝 to abstractions like 可能性、机会、体验.',
        'Avoid words whose primary industrial sense differs from the intended one: use 工期紧迫／紧急情况 not 压力 for deadline stress, 领域／行业 not 应用 for application areas, 数据／洞察 not 输入 for input, 检出率 not 检测机会 for detection performance.',
        'Give a person\'s full name in Latin script on first mention, then switch to the established Chinese transliteration (Brian Harrison → 布莱恩·哈里森，后文称哈里森). Never use a bare Latin surname as the subject of a Chinese sentence.',
        'Rewrite headlines, questions, and calls to action as idiomatic Chinese speech (问问 X、立即咨询、来现场了解) rather than literal renderings, and verify every 其／它／该 has a logically possible antecedent — never produce phrases like 将问题变为可能.',
        'Use full-width punctuation throughout Chinese text (，。、；：？！) and full-width curly quotes “ ”; never let ASCII straight quotes, half-width commas or periods appear inside a Chinese sentence.',
        'Keep terminal punctuation consistent across every parallel string in a set (bullets, feature lines, nav labels): either all end with 。 or none do. Decide once per file and apply to all.',
        'Do not stack long English pre-modifiers in front of a Chinese noun with 的. Cap a noun phrase at roughly eight characters of modifier plus one 的; move the rest into a following clause or a topic-comment structure (Topic，+ comment).',
        'Never coin nouns to mirror English abstract nominalisations. Render them as Chinese verbs or verb phrases: proximity → 就近服务, opportunities to → 可…, input from → 依据/洞察, exist to → 致力于. If the Chinese noun cannot be found in real industry writing, it is wrong.',
        'Convert English passive and participial frames into active or topic-comment Chinese: "Powered by X" → X 赋能 / 依托 X, "Built into Y" → 在 Y 中同步完成, "Trusted by Z" → 深受 Z 信赖. Avoid 由…驱动 and 被 passives unless the agent genuinely matters.',
        'Translate acronyms to the established Chinese term with the acronym in parentheses on first use (NDT → 无损检测（NDT）), then keep the Chinese term. Leave only genuinely naturalised borrowings (PLC、ADAS、AI) in Latin script.',
        'Use the specialist\'s term, not the dictionary\'s, and verify each technical noun against real Chinese industry usage: 动平衡机、盘类转子、带轴颈的转子、造纸机辊轴、轧辊表面、探头自动对中、数据采集、设备健康状态、终端用户 (not 消费者), 专业领域 (not 学科).',
        'Handle names consistently: keep company and product names in Latin script with a space on each side (…… Ascential Care ……), and never refer to a person by a bare English surname — repeat the full name or use a Chinese transliteration. Translate brand names only if the brand itself has an official Chinese name, and then use it everywhere.',
        'Use Simplified Chinese characters (简体), not Traditional (繁體).',
        'Use formal "您" when addressing the reader in B2B; "你" is too casual.',
        'Use Chinese full-width punctuation: 。 (period), ， (comma), 、 (enumeration comma), ： （ ） " " — never English . , " () in Chinese sentences.',
        'No spaces between Chinese characters; insert a single half-width space between Chinese characters and English/numbers for readability ("使用 API 接口").',
        'Numbers in B2B copy use Western digits (1,500) — Chinese numerals (一千五百) are reserved for formal/literary contexts.',
        'Use 万 (10,000) and 亿 (100M) for large numbers when culturally appropriate ("月活跃用户超 1000 万" not "月活跃用户超 10,000,000").',
        'Currency: ¥ or RMB before the number ("¥1,500" or "RMB 1,500"); 元 after ("1,500 元").',
        'Date format: YYYY年MM月DD日 (2026年4月14日) or YYYY-MM-DD.',
        'Use 24-hour time: 14:30.',
        'Translate "Learn more" as "了解更多" or "查看详情".',
        'Translate "Get started" as "立即开始" or "开始使用".',
        'Translate "Sign up" as "注册" or "免费注册".',
        'Translate "Sign in" / "Log in" as "登录"; "Sign out" / "Log out" as "退出".',
        'Translate "Free trial" as "免费试用" or "免费体验".',
        'Translate "Click here" as "点击这里" — but prefer descriptive link text.',
        'Translate "Book a demo" as "预约演示" or "申请演示".',
        'Translate "Contact us" as "联系我们".',
        'Translate "you" as "您" in B2B; never "你" by default.',
        'Translate "we" as "我们" or "本公司" / "我司" for very formal contexts.',
        'Translate "free" as "免费"; "for free" as "免费".',
        'Translate "data-driven" as "数据驱动" (commonly used) or "以数据为驱动".',
        'Translate "scalable" as "可扩展的" or "可伸缩的".',
        'Translate "ROI" as "ROI" or "投资回报率"; in B2B "ROI" alone is widely understood.',
        'Translate "stakeholder" as "利益相关者" or "干系人".',
        'Translate "case study" as "案例研究" or "成功案例" (preferred in marketing).',
        'Translate "whitepaper" as "白皮书".',
        'Translate "we help X do Y" as "我们帮助 X 实现 Y" or "我们协助 X 做 Y".',
        'Translate "Trusted by X+ companies" as "超过 X 家企业的信赖之选" or "X+ 家企业信赖之选".',
        'Translate "Powered by" as "由 X 提供技术支持" or "技术支持: X".',
        'Translate "onboarding" as "入职" (HR) or "客户引导" / "新手引导" (SaaS).',
        'Translate "subscription" as "订阅"; "billing" as "结算" or "账单".',
        'Use 的 / 地 / 得 correctly: 的 for adjectives modifying nouns (高质量的产品), 地 for adverbs modifying verbs (快速地处理), 得 for verb complements (做得很好).',
        'Avoid double negatives unless intentional — in Chinese they can come across as awkward.',
        'Use 之 for slightly more formal connections (信赖之选, 不二之选) in marketing copy.',
        'Section headers and CTAs typically have no period (。) at the end.',
        'Use 」 「 only in Traditional Chinese — Simplified uses " " or 『 』.',
        'Avoid the calque "做出意义" for "make sense" — use "有道理" or "有意义".',
    ),
    'avoid' => array(
        'Traditional Chinese characters when targeting Mainland China.',
        'English punctuation in Chinese sentences (. , " " () instead of 。 ， " " （ ）).',
        'Casual "你" in formal B2B copy.',
        'Period (。) at the end of headlines and short CTAs.',
        'Direct calques like "做出感觉" for "make sense" — use "有道理".',
        'Western metaphors that don\'t translate ("hit the ground running" — rephrase to "迅速上手").',
        'Over-translation of well-known English tech terms (API, SaaS, ROI, B2B are typically left in English).',
    ),
    'examples' => array(
        array( 'en' => 'Get started today.',                'translation' => '立即开始' ),
        array( 'en' => 'Trusted by 500+ companies.',        'translation' => '超过 500 家企业的信赖之选' ),
        array( 'en' => 'Book a demo.',                      'translation' => '预约演示' ),
        array( 'en' => 'No credit card required.',          'translation' => '无需信用卡' ),
        array( 'en' => 'Cancel anytime.',                   'translation' => '随时可取消' ),
        array( 'en' => 'Built for growing teams.',          'translation' => '为成长中的团队打造' ),
        array( 'en' => 'Save up to 40% with annual billing.', 'translation' => '年付立省 40%' ),
    ),
);
